&:2%#v_2/.@
     >3*1+.@

One hailstone step in Befunge-93, where the program counter walks a 2D grid.
& reads n, :2% tests its parity, and _ sends the cursor right (even: halve)
or left into the v (odd: down a row, then triple and add one). Every line
from here down is never visited, so it can say whatever it likes.
